            "review_text": "AnisTaib\nKuala Lumpur, Malaysia1 contribution\n0\nClean and Comfortable but bit pricy\nDec 2014 • Friends\nThis restaurant is quite clean and comfortable, the staff are friendly but food is bit quite expensive. \n\nBeside this there are some more halal restaurants in Hanoi, one nearby in Hàng Bè street, No.92 Le Duan street n some more...\n\nThose who want to buy Baju kurung, jubah, telekung and other stuff for muslim may contact murahborongvietnam.com. There design is quite nice and cheap. They have a shop in Ho Chi Minh and just opened one branch in Ha Noi. Luckily the guide took me to there shop on the 1st day the shop was opened so I got some discount.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 21, 2014",
