            "review_text": "Nurhayati_Anwar\nSurabaya10 contributions\n0\nEasy Halal Food in Hanoi\nApr 2013 • Friends\nI was not comfortable with the non halal food sold all the way in Hanoi. The smell is disturbing me because I could identify exactly the non halal ingredients. But, dont worry, Nisaa Restaurant will be your best support in Hanoi for halal food. It cost you USD 5 per meals which is quite big portion. Just call them, they will provide delivery service very fast.\n\nTips: For breakfast , you should order by phone before 10 pm, because they will not pick up your phone in the morning. Their official opening hours is 10 to 10, but they provide brekfast delivery if you prebooked it.\n\nLocated in old quarter, you may need to print a map how to find them because of the many alleys in Old Quarters.\n\nBest to Try: The Pho, Beehon Goreng, Kwe Ti Aw Goreng.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten April 21, 2013",
